  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 416.03 Scheduling of Hearings",
  "priorExpiration": "2008-07-25",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 416.03 Scheduling of Hearings.\n\n(a) Not later than 30 days after the receipt of a petition pursuant to these rules, the commissioner or a designee shall review the petition for compliance with these rules.\n\n(b) If the commissioner or designee determines that the petition complies with these rules, the petition shall be accepted.\n\n(c) If the commissioner or designee determines that the petition is not in compliance with these rules, it shall be returned to the first named petitioner, along with a statement as to the corrective action required for compliance with these rules.\n\n(d) The commissioner or designee shall schedule a public hearing to occur not later than 30 days after acceptance of a petition, unless the commissioner determines that the action requested by the petition requires compliance with RSA 270:12, in which case the hearing shall be scheduled and noticed in a manner that complies with RSA 270:12.\n\n(e) The public hearing shall be held in a town in which the lake is located.\n\nSource. #7322, eff 7-25-00; (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading) renumbered by #9211 (formerly Saf-C 414.03); EXPIRED: 7-25-08\n\nNew. (See Revision Note #2 at chapter heading) #9544, eff 9-15-09 (formerly Saf-C 415.03); ss by #12432, eff 12-11-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c400.html"
